explicit written licensing decision and replaces this file.

WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
--------------------
DocDr is a PUBLIC repository with a commercial product intent (see ROADMAP.md
and docs/MARKET_RESEARCH.md). Under the Berne Convention and GitHub's Terms of
Service, publishing a repository without a licence means all rights are
reserved by default: visitors may read and fork it, but may not lawfully
reuse, redistribute or commercialise the code.

Stating that explicitly is more honest than leaving the repository with no
LICENCE file at all, and it avoids the common failure mode where a
contributor or downstream user reasonably infers an open-source grant that was
never made.

DECISION REQUIRED (blocking for commercial release)
---------------------------------------------------
The owner must choose one of the following before public release, and replace
this file:

  1. Proprietary / all rights reserved
     - Keeps all commercial options open.
     - Contributors need a CLA; no community reuse.
     - Recommended if DocDr is intended as a paid product.

  2. Open source, weak copyleft (Apache-2.0 or MIT)
     - Maximum adoption and community trust, which suits a local-first
       privacy product.
     - Others may fork and ship competing products, including closed ones.

  3. Open source, strong copyleft (GPL-3.0)
     - Prevents closed-source forks.
     - Generally incompatible with the standard mobile app stores' terms for
       most commercial distribution; seek legal advice before choosing.

  4. Source-available (for example BSL 1.1 or a custom licence)
     - Public code, restricted commercial use, converting to open source
       later.
     - Requires licence drafting and legal review.

STATUS: DECISION PENDING - OWNER ACTION REQUIRED.

This is not a placeholder licence. No rights have been granted, and no
third-party code has been bundled. See THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md for the status of
dependencies that may be introduced later.
